+    "description": "Spec §4.8. Verify the goal's main flows end to end, add integration tests no leaf covers, sweep for unwired fields and capabilities; fix small gaps inline, file blockers for big ones.\nblocked-by ht-ma6i.1: consumes all leaves (integration sweep)\nblocked-by ht-ma6i.2: consumes all leaves (integration sweep)\nblocked-by ht-ma6i.3: consumes all leaves (integration sweep)\nblocked-by ht-ma6i.4: consumes all leaves (integration sweep)\nblocked-by ht-ma6i.5: consumes all leaves (integration sweep)\nblocked-by ht-ma6i.6: consumes all leaves (integration sweep)\nblocked-by ht-ma6i.7: consumes all leaves (integration sweep)\nblocked-by ht-ma6i.8: consumes all leaves (integration sweep)\nblocked-by ht-ma6i.9: consumes all leaves (integration sweep)\nblocked-by ht-ma6i.10: consumes all leaves (integration sweep)\nfiles: tests/ (a new integration target on an isolated Herdr session, scripts/lib/isolated-herdr.sh), Cargo.toml, .config/nextest.toml\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] On an isolated Herdr session with hook-running stand-in harnesses, a real service session: reserve, launch with the key, enroll and bind, close the pane, send refused as retired, un-retire, relaunch with the key in a new pane, same seat id, ACK deadline resumed with its remaining time, memberships intact, no re-acceptance.\n- [ ] A second agent presenting a live key leaves its pane held with no new seat, a successful hook, one alert, and the conflict visible on SeatInspect.\n- [ ] A live handoff with mixed panes resolves each per spec §4.1: bare, exited-agent, and agent with a live binding.\n- [ ] Every new field and capability is read somewhere on a production path; TRUST-POLICY's sections match what landed.\n- [ ] The test stops its processes: check-no-leaked-processes passes.\n- [ ] FinalizeRetirement over the real session settles obligations and frees the key for a new reservation.\n- [ ] Cold restart of the isolated Herdr with a keyed fresh stand-in agent reattaches the unresolved seat onto a held pane: no new seat, hold released, including a claim made during reconciliation lag with no later event.\n- [ ] Reserve-with-seat on an already-running seat, then close, un-retire, reattach by key.\n- [ ] A keyed relaunch before un-retire is held with one key_retired_reversibly alert, then reattaches on the next event after un-retire.\n- [ ] Agent exit with the pane open keeps the seat, and a relaunch keeps it (B3).\n- [ ] Seat succession: a finally retired seat's key is re-reserved onto a resolved successor with ReserveContinuityKey{key, seat}, and the old session resumed on the successor's pane checks in on the successor, with no revival of the old seat and no new seat.",
