+    "description": "Spec §4.3 cross-node. owns: the SeatRetiredReversible and SeatUnretired FactKinds, their registration and HELD_KINDS entries, materialize_seat_retired's reversible case. consumes: store::seats::reversible transitions.\nblocked-by ht-ma6i.3: consumes store::seats::reversible transitions\nfiles: src/sync/facts/seat.rs, src/sync/facts/mod.rs, src/store/materialize.rs, src/store/seats/publication.rs, src/store/seats/reversible.rs, src/store/control/retirement.rs, TRUST-POLICY.md, scripts/wire-compat-baseline.txt, tests for multinode apply\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] A published seat's reversible retirement and un-retire author the facts (needs: ht-ma6i.3); an unpublished seat authors nothing; a restore-window hold refuses them as retryable.\n- [ ] On a peer: reversible reads retired with no job; unretired restores remote and shifts that node's pending deadlines; final seat.retired on a reversible row inserts the job. A non-home origin is failed.\n- [ ] Out-of-episode facts are no-ops: a fact whose retired_at differs, and seat.retired_reversible on a finally retired row.\n- [ ] A registry without the kinds parks them, applies the final seat.retired, and after replay lands in the same state as a node that knew them, for rev/unret/rev, rev/final and rev/unret/final histories. A peer deletes its row on seat.unretired.\n- [ ] Own-log replay of a local row takes the fence's transition.\n- [ ] TRUST-POLICY: cross-node paragraph, mixed-version accepted limit, N4 authority list.\n- [ ] On a peer during the window: a send, explicit ACK recipient and invite to the seat are refused as retired, no overdue warning fires for it, and frozen rows do not starve that node's due page.\n- [ ] A message from an older node, or from a newer node before the fact arrived, reaches the home node as an ordinary fact: its receipt stays frozen with the rest, resumes on un-retire and settles on finalization.\n- [ ] After own-log restore, a keyless reversible seat keeps its reversible row and reads retired; UnretireSeat and FinalizeRetirement answer Unauthorized; operator retire finalizes it; TRUST-POLICY lists the limit.\n- [ ] project_receipt and the invitee apply write pending, with no terminal row and no terminal membership, for a fact applied during the window, on the home node and on a peer; after un-retire the obligation resumes, and after finalization it settles.",
