+    "description": "Spec §4.2 client side. owns: the one client helper that reads the variable, the key in the retained continuity intent. consumes: seat.continuity_key_v1 and the key fields on ContinuityCheckIn, ResolveSeat and CheckIn.\nblocked-by ht-ma6i.2: consumes the daemon's key decision and seat.continuity_key_v1\nfiles: src/cli/launch.rs, src/cli/handoff.rs, TRUST-POLICY.md, src/cli/hook.rs, src/cli/watch.rs, src/cli/seat_resolution.rs, src/cli/retry.rs, integrations/claude/mod/hooks/register.js, integrations/hermes/__init__.py\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] A top-level, non-subagent hook event sends the key on its C1 claim, enrollment and check-in only when the daemon advertises seat.continuity_key_v1 (needs: ht-ma6i.2).\n- [ ] A subagent, a daemon without the capability and an invalid value send nothing and print nothing.\n- [ ] A key conflict leaves the hook successful with no enrollment and no new model-visible text; the next event re-presents the key.\n- [ ] The Claude mod forwards the variable to its watch child and a watch claim carries it; the Hermes bridge has it in PANE_ENV.\n- [ ] A hook test uses CallerEnv::from_lookup, never the process env.\n- [ ] ServiceBusy on a key claim keeps the same retained intent as a C1 claim and retries on the next event, with no keyless fallback enrollment and no model-visible text.\n- [ ] The plain CLI's seat-resolving path presents the key through the one helper, and a key bound elsewhere mints no seat there; TRUST-POLICY lists that a hookless harness does not reattach by key.\n- [ ] threads' launch and handoff scrub the variable from what they start, with a test; TRUST-POLICY lists inheritance outside threads as an accepted limit.\n- [ ] The retained intent stores the key and a replay presents it; an intent recorded before the upgrade decodes as keyless; a changed key does not reuse the intent.\n- [ ] ResolveSeat presents the key only for the caller's own pane, never for launch resolving another pane.\n- [ ] A harness env passthrough that names HERDR_PANE_ID in setup or guidance (Hermes terminal.client_env_passthrough, src/harness/hermes.rs) also names the variable.",
