+    "description": "Spec §4.5, §4.2, §4.3, §4.1, §4.4. owns: schema delta 16, ContinuityKey id, ServiceSessionLevel, the service v3 types, SeatInspection optional fields, native capability constant, fact payload structs. Every other leaf consumes these. Lands only the compilable, inert boundary: tables exist, types round-trip, new service operations answer Unsupported (not advertised yet), SeatInspection fields stay None, no behaviour changes.\nfiles: migrations/node/0016_graph_clone_identity*.sql, src/store/schema.rs, src/store/seats/continuity.rs (copy helper), src/protocol/ids.rs, src/protocol/service.rs, src/protocol/results.rs, src/protocol/commands.rs, src/protocol/capabilities.rs, src/daemon/transport/service_connection.rs, src/store/service_controls.rs, src/sync/facts/seat.rs (payload types only, unregistered), scripts/wire-compat-baseline.txt\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] Migration 16 creates seat_shell_fingerprints, continuity_keys, continuity_key_conflicts, continuity_alerts, reversible_retirements (with closure_evidence and absence_evidence), restored_target_absence; adds kept_continuity_claims.continuity_key and retirements.absence_evidence; rebuilds allocation_decisions admitting structural_shell_continuity, cooperative_continuity_key, service_unretire, service_finalize (the 0012 pattern); relaxes seats_retirement_terminal only for a seat with a reversible row in state reversible.\n- [ ] A migration test from schema 15 keeps every seat, retirement and allocation decision row.\n- [ ] continuity_keys has bound_by CHECK IN ('check_in','service_reservation'); ReserveContinuityKey carries an optional seat.\n- [ ] ContinuityKey parses 1..=128 ASCII-graphic bytes and refuses anything else.\n- [ ] ServiceSessionLevel replaces the session_v2 bool and matches! list; service_session_v3 registers on this build; v1/v2 behaviour is unchanged; the five new operations round-trip and answer Unsupported.\n- [ ] ContinuityCheckIn, ResolveSeat and CheckIn carry an optional continu