+    "title": "Reversible retirement + UnretireSeat restoring memberships (D2)",
+    "description": "Design §4 D2; spec §4.3. owns: store::seats::reversible, RetirementInputs, RetirementStart, the disposition choice in begin_retirement_authored, UnretireSeat, FinalizeRetirement, service_unretire, service_finalize. consumes: store::continuity_keys seat-key lookup and key release.\nblocked-by ht-ma6i.5: consumes boundary contract\nblocked-by ht-ma6i.8: consumes store::continuity_keys seat-key lookup and key release\nboundary contract: ht-ma6i.5\nfiles: src/store/seats/reversible.rs (new), src/store/control/retirement.rs, src/store/seats/operator.rs, src/store/seats/observation.rs, src/identity/reconcile.rs, src/store/receipts.rs, src/store/poke.rs, src/store/schema.rs, src/store/service_controls.rs, TRUST-POLICY.md\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] A Closed retirement of a key-holding seat (same-incarnation close, closure proof, restored-pane close) runs the fence and writes a reversible row, no retirements row; a keyless seat is unchanged.\n- [ ] While reversible, the seat reads retired and has no retirements row and no job.\n- [ ] No overdue warning or soft poke fires; a due page full of frozen rows does not starve another seat's due row.\n- [ ] UnretireSeat by the owner: unresolved, no target, no binding, no hold change, generation bumped; another author is Unauthorized; a non-reversible seat is refused; replay is idempotent.\n- [ ] After un-retire, pending deadlines keep their remaining time, including logical receipts and invitations ; memberships and requirement episodes are effective again with no re-acceptance.\n- [ ] An unretired seat does not block hold lift and is not acted on by the reconciliation plan; its row goes on rebind and retirement.\n- [ ] FinalizeRetirement and operator seat retire on a reversible seat insert the job with the original cutover, release the key and clear its conflicts; the job settles obligations as today.\n- [ ] Operator retire and --replace of a live key-holding seat are final and release the key, so the key can be reserved again.\n- [ ] Close, un-retire, reattach, close again works: a second episode is reversible too.\n- [ ] TRUST-POLICY: Reversible retirement section, C-row text, provenance rows, accepted limits, decision record.\n- [ ] An agent exiting with its pane open leaves the seat non-retired, with no reversible row and its memberships and episodes effective, for keyless and key-holding seats, in the same incarnation and after a restart; a relaunch in that pane, with the same key or none, keeps the seat (B3).\n- [ ] FinalizeRetirement is also accepted on an unretired seat, which then retires finally.\n- [ ] Every route that writes a retirements row for a key holder releases the key and clears its conflicts, at one choke point in the disposition, with a test per route.\n- [ ] Finalization copies closure_evidence and absence_evidence from the reversible row.\n- [ ] TRUST-POLICY names as accepted limits: a seat reversibly retired or unretired whose service never acts waits for an operator (no threads timer); a keyless seat's close stays final.\n- [ ] UnretireSeat and FinalizeRetirement (reversible and unretired) work over a real service_session_v3 connection: owner authorization, operation-key replay (including a Finalize replay after the key row is gone) and payload-mismatch refusal are tested through the session.\n- [ ] After un-retire a send to the seat succeeds with the ordinary unavailable warning; retired_at, retired_seq and the structural proof are clear and a new unavailability episode is open.\n- [ ] resolution_recovery_refusal and daemon health exclude an unretired seat and suggest no rebind for it.\n- [ ] Each write-driving path of spec §4.3 composes the frozen fragment: archival (has_live_remote_member and member_active_for_archival, reversible and unretired, home node and peer) and invitation overdue and clear warning recipients, with a store test per path (fence, apply, un-retire, read). Un-retire re-bumps directory and member revisions.\n- [ ] Finalization advances retired_seq to its own decision sequence, so a fact applied during the window settles through the job rather than staying physically pending (fence, apply, finalize, read physical state).\n- [ ] TRUST-POLICY names the ACK-warning origin limit: a frozen seat misses those warnings and sees the state in pending-receipts.",
