+    "title": "Launcher-supplied continuity key on pane seats (D1)",
+    "description": "Design §4 D1; spec §4.2. owns: KeyVerdict, ContinuityEvidence::Key, cooperative_continuity_key, the conflict hold in resolution, seat.continuity_key_v1. consumes: schema delta 16, store::continuity_keys.\nblocked-by ht-ma6i.5: consumes boundary contract\nblocked-by ht-ma6i.8: consumes store::continuity_keys\nboundary contract: ht-ma6i.5\nfiles: src/store/seats/key_verdict.rs (new), src/store/seats/continuity.rs, src/store/seats/resolution.rs, src/store/seats/cooperative.rs, src/store/kept_continuity.rs, src/store/seats/observation.rs (publication cleanup), src/identity/repair.rs, src/protocol/capabilities.rs, TRUST-POLICY.md\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] Every row of the spec §4.2 table, per entry point (ContinuityCheckIn, ResolveSeat, CheckIn), is a KeyVerdict unit test and a store test.\n- [ ] A key claim reattaches an unresolved seat onto a held or unowned pane with a fresh native session, releases the hold, opens the successor binding and records cooperative_continuity_key.\n- [ ] During reconciliation lag a state-dependent answer is ServiceBusy and records no conflict.\n- [ ] A conflict is recorded through the ledger after the refused transaction rolls back (it survives the refusal), holds ordinary resolution on that target definitively (not retried under is_continuity_refusal, not kept), and clears on successful claim, target gone from a coherent publication, operator repair on the target, and key release.\n- [ ] A keyless claim behaves exactly as today, digest included; a kept claim keeps its key.\n- [ ] Unreserved and hc or named-seat keys are ignored.\n- [ ] Daemon advertises seat.continuity_key_v1.\n- [ ] TRUST-POLICY: new C1 row, provenance row, Continuity key section, decision record.\n- [ ] A first check-in or enrollment with a reserved unbound key binds it to the resolved or fresh seat with bound_by check_in on the production check-in path; a later pane close of that seat is reversible (needs: ht-ma6i.8).\n- [ ] A conflict the full table refused is still refused for that claim and is logged by the daemon; TRUST-POLICY lists the limit.\n- [ ] The conflict hold binds ordinary resolution only: C1, ht-hsyg, shell continuity and operator rebind proceed, and any rebind onto the target clears the row.\n- [ ] A conflict row on a pane with a resolved owner holds nothing: that owner's resolution and CLI keep working, tested for pane_owned_by_other_seat and seat_holds_other_key. The conflict refusal states its own cause, not restore-hold text.\n- [ ] A kept keyed claim is decided by the observation worker after lag ends with no further event: seat reattached, binding open.\n- [ ] A claimless ResolveSeat with a key bound to an unresolved seat is refused definitively with ContinuityKeyPending: no seat, no rebind, no conflict row, no alert. A plain enrollment binds a reserved unbound key.\n- [ ] key_retired_reversibly is read as the bound seat's state='retired'.\n- [ ] KeyVerdict takes whether the caller has a claim and yields Pending for the claimless refusal, per spec Key abstractions.\n- [ ] TRUST-POLICY lists the first-turn hook limit.",
