+    "title": "Seat-level shell fingerprint for live-handoff continuity (G2)",
+    "description": "Design §3 G2; spec §4.1. owns: identity::shell_continuity, seat_shell_fingerprints writes, structural_shell_continuity. consumes: schema delta 16.\nblocked-by ht-ma6i.5: consumes boundary contract\nblocked-by ht-ma6i.8: consumes the conflict-row clear in store::continuity_keys\nboundary contract: ht-ma6i.5\nfiles: src/identity/shell_continuity.rs (new), src/identity/repair.rs, src/identity/mod.rs, src/store/seats/continuity.rs, src/store/mod.rs, src/ports.rs, src/service/workers.rs, TRUST-POLICY.md\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] After a completed pass, a resolved Herdr seat with no current row gets one with pid, start, session and tty; a current row makes no Herdr call; at most 16 reads per pass with a cursor so an unreadable shell cannot starve others; named and hc seats never get one.\n- [ ] After a new incarnation, an unresolved seat with no agent binding, an exited agent, or only a managed_launch binding, whose fingerprint matches the pane shell at its saved target (pid, start, session leader, tty), resolves there unattended with kind structural_shell_continuity, hold released, no binding opened, structural proof recorded: the next reconciliation pass reconfirms the seat rather than unresolving it.\n- [ ] A seat with a live undeclined ht-hsyg candidate is left to that path; a binding is still reopened there.\n- [ ] Nothing is decided on a mismatch (new shell after cold restart, other tty, not session leader), a rival fingerprint or rival process in the pane, a kept claim on the target, a resolved owner, or a person seat. Each is a test.\n- [ ] Declines remembered 10 minutes keyed by (seat, generation, pid, start).\n- [ ] An isolated-Herdr live-handoff test covers a bare pane (also the pre-agent clone's shape), an exited-agent pane and a managed_launch-only seat.\n- [ ] TRUST-POLICY: C1 row, a new provenance row, the ht-hsyg decision record extended, the idle-agent accepted limit.\n- [ ] A key conflict row on the target does not block the decision, and the decision clears the row (needs: ht-ma6i.8).\n- [ ] TRUST-POLICY lists the no-row limit: a seat with no fingerprint row at handoff waits.\n- [ ] A fingerprint row is deleted at final retirement and at un-retire; only a non-retired seat's row is a rival; a replaced seat in a surviving shell recovers on the next handoff.\n- [ ] Allocation kicks the lane: a new bare seat gets its row with no other trigger.\n- [ ] TRUST-POLICY lists the limit for a pane process that never leads a session on a tty.",
